    twentyFirstCenturySkills: ['Critical Thinking', 'Problem Solving', 'Communication', 'Collaboration'],
    background: `Harborview Suites is a 280-room full-service commercial hotel located in Baltimore's Inner Harbor. Operating for over 18 years, the property has relied on an aging on-premise Property Management System (PMS) and legacy magnetic stripe keycards. Magnetic card replacement costs exceed $18,000 annually due to demagnetization from smartphones, while manual check-in transaction times average nearly 5.5 minutes per guest, creating persistent lobby congestion during 4:00 PM peak arrival waves.

To modernize operations and meet corporate brand mandates, ownership approved a $240,000 technology capital project: migrating from the legacy on-premise server to a modern cloud-based PMS platform and retrofitting all 280 guest room doors with Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) and Near Field Communication (NFC) digital smart locks. The upgrade promises mobile app check-in, keyless room entry via smartphone digital wallets, and real-time room status synchronization with housekeeping.

During Phase 1 beta testing across 40 suites in Tower A this past week, several severe operational flaws emerged. Nearly 20% of arriving guests attempting to use mobile Bluetooth keys experienced connection timeouts at room doors, requiring them to return to the front desk with luggage. Front-desk staff, having received only a brief 30-minute webinar on the new cloud software, struggled to re-encode physical RFID backup keycards on the new terminals, causing check-in wait times to spike to 12 minutes per guest.

Furthermore, the hard system cutover—migrating the master database of 280 in-house folios, credit card pre-authorizations, and 14,000 forward reservations—is scheduled for tonight at 2:00 AM during a Tuesday night with 84% property occupancy. The IT vendor warned that the migration requires a 90-minute complete network disconnect, during which front-desk terminals will have zero live access to guest folios, room availability, or merchant credit card processing.

The Owner and Managing Director of Harborview Hospitality (played by the judge) has summoned you and your partner (Hospitality Technology Director and Front Desk Lead) to review the cutover readiness plan. You must deliver an exhaustive Operational Cutover & Technology Troubleshooting Blueprint. Your presentation must detail the offline contingency protocol during the 2:00 AM database migration, solutions for the Bluetooth lock failure rate, a hybrid RFID/mobile key distribution policy to safeguard non-tech-savvy guests, and a comprehensive staff training matrix to ensure zero service disruption for arriving guests tomorrow morning.`,
